    {
      "id": 331,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "title": "Front, side and back to .vox",
      "pos": [
        -5080,
        90
      ],
      "size": [
        520,
        360
      ],
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Front, side and back to .vox\n1. Upload the front picture on **Front View**, the profile on **Side View** and the subject from behind on **Back View**, all with the background in alpha and at the same pixel scale.\n2. Set **side_faces** on the framing node to the way the subject faces in the side picture.\n3. Set **maximum_size** on **Save Voxel Model**: the voxels along the model's longest axis.\n4. Press **Run**, then **Download** on Save Voxel Model.\n\nNo back picture? Select **Back View** and bypass it with Ctrl+B.\n\nThe model is cropped to its bounds and saved as `output/vox/front-side_#####_.vox`. maximum_size only scales down: past TRELLIS's own resolution the model stays at that resolution, raise Trellis2UpsampleStage's resolution for more voxels."
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0
    },
